==General considerations==
* When the boat arrives, click far west on minimap to get off the boat as quickly as possible (works for both ships).
* Always fish at the double spots where possible.
* If going for points, cook your [[raw harpoonfish]] while waiting for double spots to spawn.
* Douse any [[Fire (Tempoross Cove)|fires]] using a [[bucket of water]] as soon as possible. If left unchecked, these can quickly spread. All fires will be doused by a colossal wave attack.
* Boosted [[Fishing]] levels have no effect on the rate of fishing from the [[spirit pool]], so save [[dragon harpoon]] specials for double fishing spots. Even then, the success chance maxes out at 100% at level 86 with a dragon harpoon, so there is no point boosting Fishing beyond this.
* When a colossal wave attack starts, there is plenty of time to fish 1-2 more harpoonfish before tethering, or even fix a broken tether point.
* When loading fish into crates, groups can either load one cannon per side prolonging the encounter and increasing points/experience gained per round, or alternatively, they can load both cannons on both sides to end the encounter quicker. On mass worlds it's more advantageous to only load the one cannon closest to the ship's entrance, even if it is stunned.
* When the cannon or player is stunned it takes the same amount of time to start loading again on the same cannon as it does swapping cannons.
* Tempoross will not use any of its special attacks while at 10% energy or below.
* After three rounds of draining [[Tempoross]]' energy, a message will appear in the chat box saying "Tempoross has gathered too much energy. The storm is out of control!" and the storm intensity will increase rapidly, causing the encounter to fail unless '''both''' cannons have enough fish loaded to immediately force Tempoross to submerge again.
* Upon completing a wave, use the right-click "Leave" option on the first mate to leave sooner.

==Inventory setup==
*Your inventory per game should take the following into consideration:
**[[Rope]], [[Hammer|hammers]], [[Harpoon|harpoons]], and [[Bucket|buckets]] are all available in crates as you start the minigame. 
**Rope allows you to tether yourself to the [[totem pole]]s and [[Mast (Tempoross)|mast]]s when Tempoross attacks with a colossal wave. Failing this will destroy minigame items from your inventory, costing you points and forcing you to re-obtain them. ''(Recommended 1x)'' 
**Hammer is used to repair the totem poles and masts when they break. You cannot tether if these objects are broken. ''(Recommended 1x)'' 
**Buckets of water are used to extinguish the flames from Tempoross' storm attack. Running through or being hit by a fire will destroy minigame items from your inventory forcing you to re-obtain them. Some fire arrangements will require more than one bucket of water to deal with efficiently. ''(Recommended 2x)'' 
*'''Harpoon selection'''
**While the basic [[harpoon]] can be used to catch [[harpoonfish]], players are encouraged to use one of these alternate methods if available.
***[[Barb-tail harpoon]] is the same speed as a harpoon and can be held in your main hand. This frees up an inventory slot and reduces the number of items you can lose to a wave or fire.
***Unlocking [[Bare-handed fishing|bare handed fishing]] is strongly recommended as it does not require a harpoon, is the same speed as a basic harpoon and grants additional strength experience during the minigame.
***[[Dragon harpoon]] has a special attack that increases Fishing level by +3 and will speed up gathering rates slightly.
***[[Infernal harpoon]] automatically cooks 1/3rd of all [[harpoonfish]] caught, and is the best harpoon choice when maximising point gain per hour.
***[[Crystal harpoon]] has a 1/3rd chance to catch [[crystallised harpoonfish]], and is the best harpoon choice when maximising Fishing experience gain per hour.
*'''Inventory Optimizations'''
**The full [[spirit angler's outfit]] replaces the need for a rope in your inventory, allowing you to tether without one.
**An [[Imcando hammer (off-hand)]] is recommended, as it cannot be destroyed by minigame events like the normal hammer, and can be equipped to save an inventory space.
**At low Fishing levels, an [[admiral pie]], [[fish pie]] or [[fishing potion]] can be used to increase your experience per hour significantly.
**The [[lightbearer]] ring doubles your special attack regeneration, allowing you to use the special attack of the dragon harpoon, infernal harpoon or crystal harpoon twice as often. It is the best ring slot item for point gain if you do not have level 87 Fishing (level 74 with crystal harpoon).
**If using the crystal harpoon, an [[elven signet|elven]] or [[celestial signet]] may be desired to conserve harpoon charges.

==Recommended equipment==
A good equipment setup consists of the full [[angler's outfit]] or [[spirit angler's outfit]] for the 2.5% extra Fishing experience.

Other than the experience or reward permit increase from certain harpoons and the outfits, another consideration is reducing items that could potentially be lost if hit by one of Tempoross' attacks; equipable harpoons and the [[Imcando hammer]] cannot be lost in this way, unlike a standard hammer or harpoon. Additionally, having the full Spirit Angler outfit removes the need for a rope, removing another potentially lost item and saving more inventory space.
