Cooking (permits)=
This method involves cooking all or almost all fish caught in your inventory and consistently yields 4,000–5,000 points per round and up to 6 rewards on Tempoross worlds.

===Game strategy===
When the round starts, run to the island:
* Under 85 Fishing: Catch 7 fish and then cook 7 fish. The double fishing spot should appear around the time fish 7 is cooked. Catch as many fish as possible there until the first colossal wave appears.
* Over 85 Fishing: Catch fish for 9–10 skilling ticks. If you miss a fish, stay for 10 ticks, but if you miss a fish on the 10th tick, start cooking. Your goal is to have 9 fish in your inventory when you start cooking. The double fish spot may show up sooner, but the longest it will take is the time it takes to catch and cook 9 fish, ensuring no wasted ticks. Double fish when the spot appears. Usually, the colossal wave will appear right around the time this spot ends, but you may be able to catch an extra fish or two from a single spot before you need to tether. If you fill up your inventory quickly, cook before you need to tether. Your inventory will be close to full if not full.
<br>
# Tether and when the wave dissipates, cook the remaining fish in your inventory.
# When you finish cooking the fish in your inventory, run to the boat and load/deposit all of your cooked fish into the crate by the first cannon. There is no benefit to using the second cannon or standing between the cannons.
# After you finish loading the cannon, catch as many fish as you can before 0% energy and the spirit pool opens. If you are able to get a double fishing spot before the spirit pool, cook between subsequent double fishing spots.
# At 1-2% energy, run to the dock and harpoon the spirit pool until energy recharges back up to 97–98%. '''NOTE''': You should get around 18 experience drops from the spirit pool before the next round begins.
# Cook whatever is in your inventory taking care for the third colossal wave. 
# At this point, catch and cook 7 fish at a time until a double fishing spot appears, and then alternate between double fishing and cooking. Continue until Tempoross reaches 49% energy or your inventory is full. '''NOTE''': At 49% energy you must start loading fish into the cannon or you will not have enough time to finish your inventory once the last colossal wave hits. It is possible to take Tempoross's energy down to 0% before the fourth wave but this is uncommon. If you are doing a solo run, then by having 18 fish in the cannons before he regains energy, you can defeat his 4th phase. However, he will regain energy at an accelerated rate for every phase beyond the 3rd. So it is recommended that you finish him off at this point. '''NOTE''': You may find that Tempoross already has very low health. In this case, it may be more beneficial to focus on cooking and loading fish, and skipping the final Spirit pool altogether, as you may only be able to get one or two experience drops from the final Spirit pool.
# When you finish loading your fish into the cannon, run to the dock and harpoon the spirit pool until Tempoross is defeated. 

|-|

Non-Cooking (XP)=
This method maximises experience and fish caught. You should be able to finish 2.5 to 3 inventories of fish for maximum XP per hour.

===Game strategy===
# Catch 8 fish, then run to the [[Shrine (Tempoross Cove)|shrine]] and cook them.
# When the double fishing spot spawns, fish there until the first colossal wave, tether, and then load inventory of fish to [[Ammunition crate|crate]] by the first cannon.
# Continue catching fish and load to crate again if your inventory gets full before Tempoross's energy reaches 0% and spirit pool opens. '''NOTE''': You should catch at the double fishing spot whenever possible to maximise fish caught.
# You should have close to a full second inventory before the spirit pool opens. Keep the fish in your inventory, and fish the spirit pool until Tempoross's energy reaches ~97%.
# Load fish to crate.
# Continue fishing as much as you can until Tempoross reaches ~30% energy, then load rest of the fish you caught. Finish depositing before trying to fish the spirit pool.

|-|

Solo cooking + firefighting (max permits)=
This method involves cooking all fish caught and always keeping Tempoross at low energy to prevent special attacks, while focusing on dousing fires during the final phase.<br>
Games last around 12 minutes and yield 14-18 permits (an average game yields 15-16), for a total of roughly 75-80 permits per hour.<br> 
The amount of Fishing experience per hour is dependent on the player's Fishing level. Assuming 57 fish caught and fired and 24 spirit pool scatters, the experience per game scales between ~4,000 at level 35 and ~8,900 at level 99, or about 20,000 experience per hour at level 35 and 45,000 at level 99.
