===Game strategy===
# When the round starts, immediately run to the island and begin fishing from the nearest spot.
# Catch 9 [[raw harpoonfish]], then run and begin cooking them at the [[Shrine (Tempoross Cove)|shrine]]. (Players should adjust the amount of fish they catch for this step if they find that the double fishing spot is consistently appearing either long before or after all of these initial fish have been cooked.)
# As soon as the double fishing spot appears, move to it and continue fishing. The target amount is 17 fish.
# Once 17 fish has been reached, begin cooking them if the colossal wave attack has not started yet. When the attack starts, tether to the [[totem pole]]. If already cooking, there is enough time to cook 1 or 2 more fish before tethering.
# Cook all 17 fish.
# At some point during cooking the fish and running to the ship, a storm will move in, igniting fires. It should be possible to get to the ship before any fires spawn.
# Load all cooked harpoonfish into the closest [[harpoonfish cannon]] ammunition crate. Make sure to load exactly 17. Tempoross's energy should now be at 4%, at which point no more special attacks will occur.
# Douse the flame on the ship.
# Either douse any flames that have appeared on the island to be safe, or consider leaving them to spread and only dousing them when they block your path. The latter strategy is riskier but will give more points overall. If deciding not to douse all of the fires, be wary of nearby fires jumping to the tile you're standing on while fishing or cooking.
# Catch 19 more fish, cook them all, then load them all. Make sure to do this as quickly as possible, as the timing can be tight. The highest the storm intensity can be to still leave enough time to run from the shrine to the ammunition crate is 93%. If fires block your path to the ship, you should leave at no later than 90%. If you do not succeed in catching and cooking all 19 fish in time, run to the ship and load all the cooked fish you have, keeping track of the amount. Depending on how many fish you were able to load, you may decide not to fish at the spirit pool much or at all so that you can catch and cook the remaining fish that you need. If Tempoross is not damaged to below 10% energy relatively quickly after resurfacing, a colossal wave will spawn, extinguishing all fires. In this case, you can either pivot to the "Solo Cooking" strategy or wait for another storm attack, and then immediately finish loading the amount of fish necessary to reach 19. There will still be a substantial amount of fires to put out at the end, even if the first ones get extinguished. Finally, note that it is possible to only damage Tempoross on the second and third phases and still win, so it is fine to not do any damage to him at all on the first phase if you need the maximum amount of time to get to 19 fish.
# If 19 fish were successfully loaded, damage Tempoross by fishing at the [[spirit pool]] until it regains its energy.
# For the second phase, only 19 total fish need to be caught and cooked, which is much less than the 36 needed for the first phase. Depending on how much fire has spread nearby, it may be wise to grab 5 or 10 buckets and begin putting some of them out, as you may not have time to put out all the fires during the third phase anyway. This can also be done while waiting for double fishing spots to appear. Make sure to later drop the excess buckets so that you have space for 19 fish again.
# Again before the storm intensity reaches 93%, make sure to have caught and cooked 19 fish. Then, load them all as before.
# Damage Tempoross again to at least <60%, ideally <50%.
# Fill your inventory with buckets from the crate on the dock. Run to the nearest cluster of fires, casting Humidify as you go, and begin putting them out, making your way around to the other side of the island as you do so. Keep an eye on the storm intensity, making sure you have enough time to finish off Tempoross. 
# Before the storm intensity gets too high, catch 2 more fish. They do not need to be cooked, but you can cook them if there are no more fires to be put out. Then, load them into the ammunition crate, being extra careful not to run into any fires.
# Finish Tempoross off. There may be time to put out a few more fires depending on his remaining amount of essence, but make sure to still give yourself plenty of time to win the game.

===Advanced strategy===
[[File:Tempoross Advanced Firefighting Pathing.png|thumb|Pathing for the advanced firefighting strategy.]]
A more difficult version of the firefighting strategy can be used to earn 18-21 permits per game. If done correctly, this method can earn 90-100 permits per hour. At level 99 you can expect to gain 43,000 Fishing experience, 2,000 Cooking experience, 3,000 Magic experience, and 1,000 Construction experience per hour using this method. A minimum of level 70 Fishing is recommended for consistency. An infernal harpoon will also greatly speed up the fishing sections. 

Note that the timing is tight and that stepping into a fire with an inventory full of fish will more likely than not force you to end the game early, so it is strongly recommended to have good knowledge of the normal firefighting strategy as well as decent knowledge of how fires spread. In order to allow fires to spread optimally, you should always try to leave fire to tiles it has just spread to, and where it can continue to spread from to multiple directions. Running into flames with only buckets is okay, but running into flames with any amount of harpoonfish will more likely than not end your run. If you do end up destroying harpoonfish in a fire, you can complete the game as if you were not doing the firefighting strategy to avoid completely losing the points of the botched game.

Start with filled buckets of water in the inventory leaving space for 19 harpoonfish, a rune pouch with runes for Humidify, and a rope/hammer if needed.

# When the round starts, immediately run to the island and begin fishing. (you can also grab buckets near where you spawn in and cast Humidify while running to the island)
# Catch harpoonfish until Tempoross's Energy bar reaches 95% (you should have ~10 harpoonfish by then), then cook them at the [[Shrine (Tempoross Cove)|shrine]].
# As soon as the double fishing spot appears, move to it and continue fishing until you have at least 17 fish.
# Cook at least '''17 harpoonfish'''. During this time, a colossal wave attack will happen. Tether to the [[totem pole]] to avoid being hit. If already cooking, there is enough time to cook 1 or 2 more fish before tethering.
# At some point after cooking the fish and running to the ship, a storm will move in, igniting fires. It should be possible to get to the ship before any fires spawn.
# Load 17 cooked harpoonfish into the furthest [[harpoonfish cannon]] ammunition crate, doing so will put you between the 2 crates, making it so you cannot be hit by fires spawning on the boat. '''Make sure to load exactly 17.''' Tempoross's energy should be at 4%, at which point no more special attacks will occur.
# Run back to the island. During this time, '''douse as few fires as possible and let them spread'''. It is ok to miss a double fishing spot during this time as you should have enough time to fill your inventory even at a regular fishing spot.
# Catch and cook a total of '''19 harpoonfish'''. At this point several fires should be on the island. You want to allow for fires to spread to the west of the north shrine.
# Put out most of the fires between the shrine and the ship that have spread during this time, you want to leave at least 1 fire that can still spread for later dousing. Be careful not to step into a fire at this step. Pay attention to storm intensity, you must be actively loading fish by the time the intensity bar has reached 95% or you risk failing the round entirely.
# Douse most of the fires on the ship, try to leave 1 fire that is still spreading for later dousing.
# Load all 19 cooked harpoonfish into an ammunition crate.
# Damage Tempoross by fishing at the [[spirit pool]] until it regains its energy. Fires should be spreading on the island during this time.
# Fill your inventory with buckets and cast Humidify, douse most of the fires on the island leaving 1 behind near the shrine/dock to spread for later dousing. You want to work your way west and run to the south part of the island while dousing fires and leaving 1-2 behind for spreading while you're at the other side of the island. ("P2 path" in the reference image)
# When you have made it to the south side of the island, douse fires while leaving the fire that has spread the most westward. Put out all of the fires you can around the southern shrine and dock, leaving the fires south-west of the shrine for later.
# At this point, the Storm Intensity bar should be between 40-50%. Drop buckets to make room for 19 harpoonfish (you can drop buckets between fishing actions).
# Fish and cook '''19 harpoonfish'''.
# Run to the east boat and douse all of the fires, being careful to start loading the ammunition crates before Storm Intensity reaches 95%.
# Load all 19 cooked harpoonfish.
# Fill your inventory with buckets and cast Humidify as you run back to the island. Make your way to the southern shrine. (If Tempoross is above 65% Essence at this time, go to the spirit pool and damage it below 55%)
# Douse fires along the southern edge of the island going west, wrapping back around to douse the fires that have spread from the fire left behind at step 14.
# Douse all of the fires on the entire island that have spread, making your way back to the north dock and ship.
# Fish 2-3 harpoonfish when fires have been cleared up or between dousing. You can cook the harpoonfish for slightly more points if you have time to spare.
# Douse fires on the ship that have spread, being careful to start loading the ammunition crates before Storm Intensity reaches 95%.
# Load the the closest ammunition crate with your harpoonfish and run to the dock, you should be arriving at the spirit pool right as it spawns.
# Immediately attack the pool, you will need the full attack cycle to finish off Tempoross in time.
|-|

